  "title": "Probability Decision-making Task with ambiguity",
  "description": "A multimodal dataset of human decision-making under risk and ambiguity from 53 healthy volunteers aged 18-31. It includes structural MRI (T1w, T2w, DWI), task fMRI, and concurrent EEG recorded during inhibitory transcranial magnetic stimulation over two parietal regions and the vertex. The data enable investigation of the role of the parietal cortex in ambiguity computations.",
  "methods_description": "Participants performed a probability decision-making task with risk and ambiguity conditions during fMRI acquisition. EEG was recorded concurrently with inhibitory TMS applied over two parietal regions and the vertex. Structural MRI included T1w, T2w, and diffusion-weighted imaging.",
